  {
   "@id": "http://localhost:8080/how-much-do-movers-cost-houston/#faq",
   "@type": "FAQPage",
   "mainEntity": [
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A studio move costs $280–$740 and a 1-bedroom move $380–$960, at 10 road miles, off peak, with no stairs or extras, with 2 movers at $100–$150 an hour. On a job this small, a minimum number of hours or a trip fee can matter as much as the rate, so how much do movers cost Houston renters depends on those terms too."
     },
     "name": "How much do movers cost Houston renters for a small apartment?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Not always. A flat rate, set after the mover sees your things, shields you from traffic and a slow day, while an hourly rate can come out lower for a small move you've packed and staged well. Compare both on the same inventory, because how much do movers cost Houston households under either one depends on what's listed."
     },
     "name": "Is a flat-rate quote cheaper than hourly movers in Houston?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "It can save money if you're happy to drive. A labor-only crew of 2 costs $80–$130 an hour to load or unload a truck you rent, so you pay for the truck, fuel and your own time instead of a full crew. It works best for a short move, and it lowers how much do movers cost Houston renters most when the crew only needs a couple of hours."
     },
     "name": "Should you rent a truck and hire loaders in Houston?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Tipping is up to you. Guides suggest a tip per mover by the hour or for the day, or a share of the bill, and many suggest a bit more for heat, stairs or heavy pieces. The tip calculator on this page works those published ranges out for your crew and hours."
     },
     "name": "How much should you tip movers after a hot Houston move?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Look up its certificate number in the TxDMV's Truck Stop to make sure it is licensed, and read recent reviews for how it handled problems. Ask for a written proposal and the Texas rights sheet, and be wary of a price far below the others."
     },
     "name": "How do you check a Houston mover before you book?"
    }
   ]
  }
